  "id": "COMPOUND:11699 - PROTEIN:3966",
  "verbalization": "Anethole trithione appears to exert its biological effects through a shared pathway involving Phytolaccoside B, which acts as a target for multiple kinases, including Tyrosine-protein kinase CSK and Serine/threonine-protein kinase ULK3. Both of these kinases are ultimately targeted by Phytolaccoside B, which in turn interacts with Receptor-type tyrosine-protein phosphatase beta. This suggests that Anethole trithione may influence the activity of these kinases, potentially modulating the function of the phosphatase receptor. The evidence indicates a direct or indirect relationship between Anethole trithione and the receptor, mediated through Phytolaccoside B. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Anethole trithione could affect receptor activity, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
